#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md:6
msgid "The `proc_macro` Crate"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md:8
msgid ""
"The compiler-provided `proc_macro` crate defines the primary low-level types "
"for procedural macro manipulation. These are the actual types underlying the "
"tokens we match in declarative macros:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md:12
msgid "**`TokenStream`:** An iterator over a sequence of `TokenTree` values."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md:13
msgid ""
"**`TokenTree`:** An enum representing individual lexical units. It has four "
"variants:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md:15
msgid "`Group`: A bracketed group of tokens (e.g., `(a + b)`, `{ ... }`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md:16
msgid "`Ident`: An identifier or keyword (e.g., `foo`, `fn`, `let`, `false`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md:17
msgid ""
"`Punct`: A single punctuation character (e.g., `+`, `,`, `:`, but _not_ "
"combined operators like `+=`, nor brackets)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md:19
msgid "`Literal`: A literal value (e.g., `\"hello\"`, `42`, `3.14`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md:32
msgid ""
"Discuss that `proc_macro` is a built-in crate, so you don't need to add it "
"to your `Cargo.toml` dependencies (just defining `proc-macro = true` makes "
"it automatically available)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md:35
msgid ""
"`TokenStream` can be converted to and from strings via `to_string()` and "
"`parse()`, but doing so breaks its relation to its original source code "
"location (`Span`), which should be preserved so compiler error messages can "
"point at the relevant code."
msgstr ""
